> I like the idea. Chains should make more damage, and damage even thick
> skinned monsters, yes.

Chains are heavy.  Damage by wielded objects is based on their
weight and I don't think it's limited to thin skinned monsters.
Consider that the heavy iron ball from punishment is a good
weapon as long as your choice is to carry it or drag it but not
leave it behind.  Since chains are heavy they should work fine
as weapons.

> I don't think that they should be effective in
> grabbing items, though.

I recall at least one scene in a Samurai movie where a Samurai
uses a chain to disarm another Samurai or at least to damage
his opponent's katana.  I don't think the chance should be high
but making it available does make sense in terms of that movie
scene.  I think it was in The Samurai Trilogy - Myamoto Musashi
as Marvin?

